# session state (Claude Code local settings/permissions) — per-machine, never
# project record. Also covered by the user's global ignore on this machine;
# this line makes the decision durable in-repo (TASK 0, B-2026-08-21-C).
.claude/

# handoff channel — seat MAIL stays off-repo, but THE_BUILD and THE_BUILD_REPORT
# are not mail: they are the project's only record of what was built and what was
# seen, overwritten each build — uncommitted, "git carries the history" is false.
# (mothership ruling, 2026-08-21: the ignore yields for exactly these two paths.)
# THE_SEAT_MAP is DOCTRINE, not mail — an untracked file is an unprotected file
# (B-101 §3, ratified by Arman: "you are our sixth mothership. ratified. proceed.")
# THE_SUBSTRATE_MAP is doctrine by the same law (B-106 A1): every seat reads it
# at wake, so it is protected like the seat map — the ignore yields for it too.
# `.handoff/*`, NOT `.handoff/` — same reason as instruments/* below: git will
# not descend into an excluded directory, so the negations would silently fail.
# THE PROTECTED RECORD (U1, ratified by Arman 2026-08-29: "track the record's
# seven-odd files"): a STANDING ASSERTION is tracked; a DATED EVENT is not.
# Ledgers, plans and doctrine are standing assertions — re-read and amended,
# and a successor seat must RE-GROUND from them (a successor cannot re-ground
# from a file that is not in the tree). Mail, reports, drafts, plates and
# audits are dated events: true when written, never amended, and the tracked
# pair above already carries what the record needs from them. The next
# `.handoff` file decides for itself which side it falls on.
.handoff/*
!.handoff/THE_BUILD.md
!.handoff/THE_BUILD_REPORT.md
!.handoff/THE_SEAT_MAP.md
!.handoff/THE_SUBSTRATE_MAP.md
!.handoff/THE_SOVEREIGN_LEDGER.md
